# Two branches that both add an entry under `## [Unreleased]` conflict on every
# merge, and the resolution is always the same: keep both entries. That is what
# the union driver does, so it does it rather than a person doing it by hand
# once per branch per day. The entries are whole paragraphs separated by blank
# lines, so a union keeps each one intact and only the order of the two blocks
# is decided by which side git reads first, which the release notes reorder
# anyway.
#
# Nothing else in the tree gets this. A union merge on source is how you get a
# file that contains both halves of a disagreement and compiles.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
